(registered 2026-11-18, last updated 2026-11-18)

Media type name: application

Media subtype name: vnd.colabox.fppd+json

Required parameters: N/A

Optional parameters: N/A

Encoding considerations: binary

UTF-8 encoded JSON text (RFC 8259); lines may exceed 998 octets.

Security considerations: The media type contains no active or
executable content. It is a JSON document describing a quilt block
design: line geometry, colours, numeric settings, and
optionally one embedded reference image as a base64 data URL
(image/png or image/jpeg).

The content does not require privacy or integrity services beyond
those of the transport; the format itself provides none. A file may
contain a user's own photograph, so users should
treat files as personal content when sharing.

If protection is wanted, TLS is recommended for files in transit
(for example, HTTPS; see BCP 195). For files that are stored, or that
pass through intermediaries such as email or cloud
storage, JSON Object Signing and Encryption (JOSE) is the preferred
mechanism, because the payload is a JSON document. JSON Web Encryption
(RFC 7516) provides confidentiality and
integrity. JSON Web Signature (RFC 7515) provides integrity and,
when a digital signature is used, authenticity of origin. The whole
file is used as the JOSE payload, and the "cty" header
parameter may be set to "vnd.colabox.fppd+json". The result is a
JOSE object, not a document of this media type, and it must be
decrypted or verified before it is processed as one.
Readers of this media type are not required to support these mechanisms.

The security considerations of JSON (RFC 8259, section 12) apply.
Readers should validate all numeric values and array sizes, and should
limit the decoded size of the embedded image
before decoding it, to avoid resource exhaustion. The image must be
processed only by a safe image decoder.

The format does not use compression itself; the embedded image uses
PNG or JPEG compression, whose decoder considerations apply.

No container format is used.

The "spec" member contains the URL of the specification for
information only; no links need to be dereferenced to interpret the
content.

Interoperability considerations: Files are UTF-8 JSON objects. They are identified by the top-level member "format" with the value "fpp-studio-pattern" and an integer "version" (currently 2). Readers must ignore unknown members and must refuse files whose "format" member has another value. Earlier files without a "format" member (version 1, extension .ppd) may still be accepted by readers.

Published specification: https://colabox.net/fppd

Applications which use this media: FPP Studio (Android), a foundation paper piecing (FPP) quilt pattern designer by Colabox Studio, uses this type to save, share and open pattern files. A web version is planned.

Fragment identifier considerations: N/A

Restrictions on usage: N/A

Additional information:

1. Deprecated alias names for this type: N/A
2. Magic number(s): The file begins with the bytes {"format":"fpp-studio-pattern"
3. File extension(s): fppd
4. Macintosh file type code: N/A
5. Object Identifiers: N/A

